  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 210 AM EDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nCanadian High pressure settles overhead beneath a persistent \nnorthwest flow aloft. While the larger scale upper-level pattern\nmay fluctuate somewhat with time, little overall change is \nexpected through much of the forecast period, favoring a \ncontinued stretch of generally dry and seasonable temperatures \nwith increasing temperatures, humidity, and shower chances as we\nget to the latter half of the week. \n\nWinds will continue to ease as high pressure works overhead, \nallowing for efficient radiational cooling... Featuring more of \nthe same with cooler overnight temperatures (like last night) \nexpected for tonight across the traditional colder interior \nlocations. Overnight lows could dip into the low 50s to upper \n40s before quickly rebounding after sunrise. Despite the cool \nstarts, afternoon temperatures today and Thursday should \nsteadily moderate with locations climbing back into the 70s and \n80s under plentiful sunshine. \n\nAttention then turns toward late week into the weekend as \nnorthwest flow persists and a couple of subtle disturbances \nattempt to work southeast across the Upper Great Lakes. \nConfidence remains lower regarding the timing and coverage of \nany precipitation, though the current signal continues to favor \nat least low chances for scattered showers and perhaps a few \nthunderstorms sometime Friday into Saturday...Stay tuned!",
